{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03NJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{\\varphi_i : U_i \\to U\\}_{i\\in I} \\in \\text{Cov} (\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}(U) \\longrightarrow \\prod\\nolimits_{i\\in I} \\mathcal{F}(U_i)\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$s \\mapsto (s|_{U_i})_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{\\varphi_i : U_i \\to U\\}_{i\\in I} \\in \\text{Cov} (\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0008": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-sheaf-axiom}\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{F}(U) \\ar[r] &\n\\prod_{i\\in I} \\mathcal{F}(U_i) \\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r] &\n\\prod_{i, j \\in I} \\mathcal{F}(U_i \\times_U U_j),\n}\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0009": "$s \\mapsto (s|_{U_i})_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0010": "$(s_i)_{i\\in I} \\mapsto (s_i |_{U_i \\times_U U_j})$", "MATH_0011": "$(s_i)_{i\\in I} \\mapsto (s_j |_{U_i \\times_U U_j})$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c36a2db041c810a98dffcb45432178a17f096eef8965b06f8957ad7aab3cffbf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d0ae0d7542b2b27bb0b2b43eacd8ad4de3df0b227442e3bf4bf4f38b66903b1e", "source_text": "A presheaf <MATH_0001> of sets (resp. abelian presheaf) on a site\n<MATH_0002> is said to be a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>separated presheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for all coverings\n<MATH_0003>\nthe map\n<MATH_0004>\nis injective. Here the map is <MATH_0005>.\nThe presheaf <MATH_0006> is a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>sheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if for all coverings\n<MATH_0007>, the\ndiagram\n<MATH_0008>\nwhere the first map is <MATH_0009> and the two\nmaps on the right are\n<MATH_0010> and\n<MATH_0011>,\nis an equalizer diagram in the category of sets (resp.<SPACE_0001>abelian groups).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:43fc632c847255897a8c500e757534014ff75da8a89c4cde10dc89a0ab1aed9e", "unit_id": "tag:03NK:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "03NJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$I = \\emptyset$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}(\\emptyset)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\textit{Ab}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-empty-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:77965c8af2803cdd63fc685ceabf78ffe3e810afea6ad67a2df078e87d4ffcd4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0c1d5d3161b652f10c085dc93abff0c59fea9d93a78e6e2e1221db15cefa2406", "source_text": "For the empty covering (where <MATH_0001>), this implies that\n<MATH_0002> is an empty product, which is a final object in the\ncorresponding category (a singleton, for both <MATH_0003> and\n<MATH_0004>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2cc00be56b5004f50cf33eb98d931d22dcb2338966f28b8f8c66e9caad92894e", "unit_id": "tag:03NM:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "03NJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X_{Zar}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-site-topological-space}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-sheaf-site-space}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:49c7f241563ece5d1f256348c380953ac0d99432d9b9dd147c6a2768e3c53549", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3aec8e236d6a04d653c05a44ff389dd91f30da2e344e56d64c9ae1ff4b235f37", "source_text": "Working this out for the site <MATH_0001> associated to a topological\nspace, see Example <REF_0001>, gives the usual\nnotion of sheaves.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:989ec6410e90e7bb18e8d3787b839140e0de7d69098c6d7c5378b39ed73343a7", "unit_id": "tag:03NN:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03NJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{Ab}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\textit{PAb}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "SPACE_0003": "\\ ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-category-sheaves}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dc7b945b9ae86e4ed2a6fbe780b6797f7fc85e8e87611801567b1c99bb311932", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:70befa5b309de6718f2d73805a093a3ea5d01f3a08d4e4d5bb70453bebb5597a", "source_text": "We denote <MATH_0001> (resp.<SPACE_0001><MATH_0002>)\nthe full subcategory of <MATH_0003>\n(resp.<SPACE_0002><MATH_0004>) whose objects are sheaves. This is the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>category of sheaves of sets<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> (resp.<SPACE_0003><TEXTITOPEN_0002>abelian sheaves<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>) on\n<MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c2d9a8dbc2e400f45792823abc32ad37d2dafb0fd2bd1a662df1ba79a5dfc418", "unit_id": "tag:03NO:statement"}
